fixNote:"Your original has curly quotes and en-dashes (–s, –am, –u) pasted from Word. A terminal rejects them, so the corrected version uses plain \" and -. Also, git switch master only works if your first branch is called master. If git init made main, use that name. Also, file.py is staged but never committed, so git push does not upload it.",
steps:[["3","git init","Creates a hidden .git folder so Git starts tracking this folder."],["4-5","git config --global ...","Stores your name and email. Every commit carries them."],["7","git add .","Stages all changed files for the next commit. The dot means everything here."],["8","git status -s","Short status: A = added, ?? = untracked."],["12","git commit -am","Saves a snapshot with the message Done. -a stages tracked files, -m adds the message."],["14-15","git branch main / git switch main","Makes a new branch called main and moves onto it."],["19-20","git switch master / git merge main","Go back to master and bring the work from main into it."],["22-23","git remote add / git push -u","Links your GitHub repo as origin, then uploads master and remembers it."],["24","git pull","Downloads and merges new changes from GitHub."]],
